{"batch": "supplement-records", "id": "Agrotechny-new-record", "key": "Agrotechny", "disposition": "applied", "drafted": "by hand", "rule": "every 1913 entry gets a record; supplement entries the 1907 printing lacks take Webster's New International Dictionary as their print witness, accepted only where it matches Gutenberg word for word", "new": "<h2 d:priority=\"2\" class=\"hw\">Ag&#x2032;ro-tech&#x2CA;ny</h2>, <div class=\"pos\">noun </div><div d:priority=\"2\" class=\"ety\">[Gr. <div class=\"grk\">&#x1F00;&#x3B3;&#x3C1;&#x3CC;&#x3C2; </div>field, land + <div class=\"grk\">&#x3C4;&#x3AD;&#x3C7;&#x3BD;&#x3B7; </div>an art.] </div><div class=\"def\">That branch of agriculture dealing with the methods of conversion of agricultural products into manufactured articles; agricultural technology.</div><br/> ", "newSha256": "afb4e473803ace705dd5cbf9eb850e9e0103241a83c42b555db99c3a18703285", "inventoryRow": "supplement:670:1466", "templates": ["Agrostology", "Agrostography", "Futurist"], "witness": "1915 New International (archive.org bwb_O8-DDQ-914) leaf 149, p. 47; 1914 London New International vol. 1 (gacr_…vol-1…) leaf 137", "absentFrom1907": "1900 Supplement, 1907 Merriam printing (HathiTrust uiug.30112099825041) scan 1129, p. 9, runs Agrestial, Agrostemma, Agrypnia, Agua", "readings": [{"reader": "Opus, 1915 strip, blind", "strip": "s3", "linesSha256": "8568aad9475fef26f0f8e3a5679cd430edd2d266c0ec20a758c817c60eaf0ea7"}, {"reader": "Opus, 1915 strip, blind", "strip": "s3", "linesSha256": "8568aad9475fef26f0f8e3a5679cd430edd2d266c0ec20a758c817c60eaf0ea7"}, {"reader": "Opus, 1914 London strip, blind", "strip": "t3", "linesSha256": "61dfe6af3065c027fbb575206a1dbb0443fb95d99897656a5c00e343a73a80c7"}], "stripBoxes": {"s3": {"source": "/Users/nicktrombley/Code/websters-api/.context/dictionary-audit/supplement-records/nid/pages/1915-n149.jpg", "sourceSha256": "03d8c3e52ac2230926f451c7bbd7fe3a18b1fa3107abe8bab0e477c09cef7231", "box": [135, 1720, 930, 1862], "scale": 1.89, "size": [1500, 267], "stripSha256": "391862a80ae95a253400c79fd12aa1bb34350451a88c06475de2dba85307e44c"}, "t3": {"source": "/Users/nicktrombley/Code/websters-api/.context/dictionary-audit/supplement-records/nid/pages/1914v1-n137.jpg", "sourceSha256": "438e03fbcf9cd0bd8030c451ff70c102029d9c5f4df994888256af750bde723b", "box": [135, 1676, 910, 1810], "scale": 1.94, "size": [1500, 259], "stripSha256": "a09af072509d1f21ea9a11d13308e56f3a12db48611912a2c5c2cad2c230261a"}}, "note": "The New International prints \"[Gr. ἀγρός field, land + τέχνη an art.]\" where Gutenberg has \"&?;\" for both Greek words. LSJ attests ἀγρός \"field\" and τέχνη \"art\" with these accents and breathing. Headword notation from Gutenberg (Ag\"ro*tech`ny). Pronunciation left out: the 1915 readers read (ăg′rȯ-tĕk′nĭ) and the 1914 reader (ăg′rō-tĕk′nĭ), and ȯ is the New International's mark."}
{"batch": "supplement-records", "id": "Fuselage-new-record", "key": "Fuselage", "disposition": "applied", "drafted": "by hand", "rule": "every 1913 entry gets a record; supplement entries the 1907 printing lacks take Webster's New International Dictionary as their print witness, accepted only where it matches Gutenberg word for word", "new": "<h2 d:priority=\"2\" class=\"hw\">Fu&#x2032;se-lage</h2>, <div class=\"pos\">noun </div><div class=\"fld\">(Ae&#x308;ronautics) </div><div class=\"def\">An elongated body or frame of an ae&#x308;roplane or flying machine; sometimes, erroneously, any kind of frame or body. Many ae&#x308;roplanes have no fuselage, properly so called.</div><br/> ", "newSha256": "1eba2b4790153313d58f853c52c103b8420aa1c837ba226e800d994223a515e3", "inventoryRow": "supplement:670:3606", "templates": ["Biplane", "Futurist", "Aileron"], "witness": "1915 New International leaf 101 (Addenda of new words); 1914 London New International vol. 1 leaf 89 (Addenda)", "absentFrom1907": "in the New International's Addenda of new words (copyright 1913), so not in the 1909 New International vocabulary and absent from the 1907 printing", "readings": [{"reader": "Opus, 1915 strip, blind", "strip": "s1", "linesSha256": "bfca60b92c178eb7f134dcba1484303a5028e6e56a941ac49d7d050f2063e11f"}, {"reader": "Opus, 1915 strip, blind", "strip": "s1", "linesSha256": "4246a9d768dd53421c51f554415aec0b1eb1a5c8075fe84b6effff7b27ea2bd0"}, {"reader": "Opus, 1914 London strip, blind", "strip": "t1", "linesSha256": "d3b99708eb1f39c5b09bc5132ed21090c39c81e868ac55fb8fbc12bad1826097"}], "stripBoxes": {"s1": {"source": "/Users/nicktrombley/Code/websters-api/.context/dictionary-audit/supplement-records/nid/pages/1915-n101.jpg", "sourceSha256": "9998b0e17e6da4fdd710785b72fdfe1f9f13ad887fc6614049f25450cd96bab1", "box": [900, 1815, 1695, 2028], "scale": 1.89, "size": [1500, 401], "stripSha256": "a6bfcef980b4dde3187a9f19fbf577598e846aebca38f1bef57d9709e8e8ae45"}, "t1": {"source": "/Users/nicktrombley/Code/websters-api/.context/dictionary-audit/supplement-records/nid/pages/1914v1-n89.jpg", "sourceSha256": "86d79b387604ee00eb91a4c64679be170a23f7f189ef1ebc557390358f0fc704", "box": [895, 1790, 1700, 1996], "scale": 1.86, "size": [1500, 383], "stripSha256": "5beeff062ccf036702b5502876a8aa0ef7b18010f554e5d56138174cfd56a0d6"}}, "note": "House style: the New International adds \"[F.]\", sets \"so-called\" and an unparenthesized field label; the record follows Gutenberg (\"properly so called\", \"(Aëronautics)\", no etymology). Pronunciation left out: readers split on the last vowel (läj, lȧj)."}
{"batch": "supplement-records", "id": "Futurism-new-record", "key": "Futurism", "disposition": "applied", "drafted": "by hand", "rule": "every 1913 entry gets a record; supplement entries the 1907 printing lacks take Webster's New International Dictionary as their print witness, accepted only where it matches Gutenberg word for word", "new": "<h2 d:priority=\"2\" class=\"hw\">Fu&#x2032;tur-ism</h2>, <div class=\"pos\">noun </div><div class=\"fld\">(Painting) </div><div class=\"def\">A movement or phase of post-impressionism (which see, below).</div><br/> ", "newSha256": "f6ad58997442408c74b7beeb39a50cbeae2bcd30710f93685759b074a67b87f4", "inventoryRow": "supplement:670:3613", "templates": ["Cubism", "Futurist"], "witness": "1915 New International leaf 101 (Addenda); 1914 London vol. 1 leaf 89 (Addenda)", "absentFrom1907": "in the New International's Addenda of new words (copyright 1913)", "readings": [{"reader": "Opus, 1915 strip, blind", "strip": "s1", "linesSha256": "bfca60b92c178eb7f134dcba1484303a5028e6e56a941ac49d7d050f2063e11f"}, {"reader": "Opus, 1915 strip, blind", "strip": "s1", "linesSha256": "4246a9d768dd53421c51f554415aec0b1eb1a5c8075fe84b6effff7b27ea2bd0"}, {"reader": "Opus, 1914 London strip, blind", "strip": "t1", "linesSha256": "d3b99708eb1f39c5b09bc5132ed21090c39c81e868ac55fb8fbc12bad1826097"}], "stripBoxes": {"s1": {"source": "/Users/nicktrombley/Code/websters-api/.context/dictionary-audit/supplement-records/nid/pages/1915-n101.jpg", "sourceSha256": "9998b0e17e6da4fdd710785b72fdfe1f9f13ad887fc6614049f25450cd96bab1", "box": [900, 1815, 1695, 2028], "scale": 1.89, "size": [1500, 401], "stripSha256": "a6bfcef980b4dde3187a9f19fbf577598e846aebca38f1bef57d9709e8e8ae45"}, "t1": {"source": "/Users/nicktrombley/Code/websters-api/.context/dictionary-audit/supplement-records/nid/pages/1914v1-n89.jpg", "sourceSha256": "86d79b387604ee00eb91a4c64679be170a23f7f189ef1ebc557390358f0fc704", "box": [895, 1790, 1700, 1996], "scale": 1.86, "size": [1500, 383], "stripSha256": "5beeff062ccf036702b5502876a8aa0ef7b18010f554e5d56138174cfd56a0d6"}}, "note": "House style: the New International closes \"postimpressionism\"; the record follows Gutenberg's \"post-impressionism\", the record's own Post-impressionism key. Pronunciation left out: readers split on the mark under t."}
{"batch": "supplement-records", "id": "Movie-new-record", "key": "Movie", "disposition": "applied", "drafted": "by hand", "rule": "every 1913 entry gets a record; supplement entries the 1907 printing lacks take Webster's New International Dictionary as their print witness, accepted only where it matches Gutenberg word for word", "new": "<h2 d:priority=\"2\" class=\"hw\">Mov&#x2032;ie </h2><div class=\"pr\">(moo&#x35E;v&#x2032;i&#x306;)</div>, <div class=\"pos\">noun </div><div class=\"def\">A moving picture or a moving picture show; &#x2014; commonly used in <i class=\"it\">pl.</i> </div><div class=\"mark\">[Slang or Colloq.]</div><br/> ", "newSha256": "2a81cf335f390142acf9c78229d244d413ffcf304996eaed8bfebd04ac1f50d3", "inventoryRow": "supplement:670:4869", "templates": ["Movable", "Highbinder", "Dopy"], "witness": "1915 New International leaf 102 (Addenda); 1914 London vol. 1 leaf 90 (Addenda)", "absentFrom1907": "in the New International's Addenda of new words (copyright 1913)", "readings": [{"reader": "Opus, 1915 strip, blind", "strip": "s2", "linesSha256": "aed122437b91aff6131a67445dfb9fe986022d24f0dcae2093a2651889ec54dd"}, {"reader": "Opus, 1915 strip, blind", "strip": "s2", "linesSha256": "9a1c15ea660df4b2aa09d5c01a86739df00e7e53261244f7dbee1a20abfa0c44"}, {"reader": "Opus, 1914 London strip, blind", "strip": "t2", "linesSha256": "97fb70f4ae3ee51833d6b409436dda90e1946cab8f14bc512f652e9302bb9c21"}], "stripBoxes": {"s2": {"source": "/Users/nicktrombley/Code/websters-api/.context/dictionary-audit/supplement-records/nid/pages/1915-n102.jpg", "sourceSha256": "206e50780a7d6defa68030201f1a10b34ebbba57e46f09dfee44f5ced4ed6c7f", "box": [40, 1945, 840, 2190], "scale": 1.88, "size": [1500, 459], "stripSha256": "b566192c5f77e42e2f124a6db98261b7f158380da0ec8850555022348548c3f4"}, "t2": {"source": "/Users/nicktrombley/Code/websters-api/.context/dictionary-audit/supplement-records/nid/pages/1914v1-n90.jpg", "sourceSha256": "d7bd5ad395ca21299506170f9bd27c6dc063681df61d4057a5f4192854677a37", "box": [30, 1895, 805, 2140], "scale": 1.94, "size": [1500, 474], "stripSha256": "8f675032bc64c46ec0776916d8b053cb4796dfad1a98c996fa43358f101359a1"}}, "note": "Pronunciation (mo͞ov′ĭ): two readers wrote o + U+035E + o, the third two macrons over the oo; written in the corpus form moo&#x35E;v. \"[Slang or Colloq.]\" takes Gutenberg's brackets."}
